# Fix ts_project validation on Windows with the rules_js hermetic launcher
# (--@aspect_rules_js//js:use_hermetic_launcher, set in common.bazelrc).
# The validator unconditionally replaced every backslash in its JSON argument with a quote,
# a workaround for the .bat launcher stripping quotes. The hermetic launcher (validator.exe)
# preserves them, so {\"a\":1} became {""a"":1} and JSON.parse failed with
# "Expected ':' after property name in JSON at position 3".
# Now escaped quotes are unescaped first, and the blanket replacement is only a fallback.
--- a/ts/private/ts_project_options_validator.cjs
+++ b/ts/private/ts_project_options_validator.cjs
@@ -130,15 +130,26 @@
